From 9d6ebbd62b586f7fe632c9b2feb2dd1c2ea65b86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:08:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(post): refuse a preset above the machine's last
 preset row

The two Heidenhain posts accepted presets 1..6. The Picomax 55 preset
table on the 2008 delivery CD has rows 0..5 only, so Q339=+6 names a
row that does not exist and the control stops with an alarm.

A machine file can now state controller.work_offset_max, the highest
work offset that the control holds. The reader and the raw engine
refuse a value that is not a whole number from 1 to 255. The mirror
carries the key. The post engine refuses a higher PARAM WorkOffset by
setup name before any hook runs, for each post. A machine without the
key keeps the post's own limit. fehlmann-picomax55.mch states 5.

Fixes #4088

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
